From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 22:54:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vrend: check for a host GL error once per command buffer

The decoder calls glGetError() after every decoded command. In a build that
treats a host GL error as fatal that is what names the offending command, but
this project builds with -Dcheck-gl-errors=false, where the check can only
warn and can never fail a command - and glGetError() is a synchronizing query.

On the Zink provider Mesa marshals GL calls to a worker thread, so every one
of those queries runs _mesa_glthread_finish(): it drains the marshal buffer
and unmarshals it on the decoder's own thread. A command buffer of 2048 draws
therefore pays 2048 synchronizations, and the decoder can never run ahead of
the driver. A profile of a 2048-draw frame put 4.6% of the renderer thread
inside glGetError's synchronization alone, with the whole GL pipeline
executing underneath it instead of on the worker thread.

Keep the per-command check where it is meaningful, and drain the error queue
once per command buffer otherwise: a host GL error is still reported and the
driver's queue stays bounded; only the name of the command that raised it is
lost, in a build that was never going to act on it.
---
 src/vrend/vrend_decode.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/vrend/vrend_decode.c b/src/vrend/vrend_decode.c
index 71cf1aff031ba8711616e288f718bc67dc3c11cb..eafbab0aa0ffec8b34d15482b6553e863ba733e5 100644
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_decode.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_decode.c
@@ -21,6 +21,10 @@
  * OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.
  *
  **************************************************************************/
+#ifdef HAVE_CONFIG_H
+#include "config.h"
+#endif
+
 #include <stdint.h>
 #include <string.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
@@ -2115,8 +2119,19 @@ static int vrend_decode_ctx_submit_cmd(struct virgl_context *ctx,
       TRACE_SCOPE_SLOW(vrend_get_comand_name(cmd));
 
       ret = decode_table[cmd](gdctx->grctx, buf, len);
+#ifdef CHECK_GL_ERRORS
+      /* Naming the command that produced a host GL error is worth a
+       * glGetError() per command only in a build that treats such an error as
+       * fatal. Everywhere else the check can only warn, and glGetError() is a
+       * synchronizing query: on a host GL stack that marshals its calls to a
+       * worker thread (Mesa's glthread, which the Zink provider uses) every
+       * call drains the marshal buffer and runs it on this thread, so a
+       * command buffer of 2048 draws pays 2048 synchronizations and the
+       * renderer never runs ahead of the driver at all.
+       */
       if (!vrend_check_no_error(gdctx->grctx) && !ret)
          ret = EINVAL;
+#endif
       if (ret) {
          virgl_error("context %d failed to dispatch %s: %d\n",
                gdctx->base.ctx_id, vrend_get_comand_name(cmd), ret);
@@ -2136,6 +2151,13 @@ static int vrend_decode_ctx_submit_cmd(struct virgl_context *ctx,
     * guest the rest of its session.
     */
    vrend_clear_context_error(gdctx->grctx);
+#ifndef CHECK_GL_ERRORS
+   /* One drain per command buffer still reports a host GL error and still
+    * keeps the driver's error queue bounded; only the name of the command
+    * that raised it is lost.
+    */
+   vrend_check_no_error(gdctx->grctx);
+#endif
    return ret;
 }
 
